    )", "explanation": "Replace the deprecated v1 nested `class Config(ExampleConfigDefaults): pass` with `model_config = ConfigDict(...)`, per the migration guide (Changes to config). The keys from ExampleConfigDefaults are carried over unchanged. Dunder attributes are filtered out so only the config keys are passed to ConfigDict."}], "notes": "The finding is addressed with two edits: the ConfigDict import, and replacing the nested class Config with model_config. ExampleConfigDefaults is defined outside the files I was given (pydantic_cli/examples/__init__.py is not in the migration list), so I could not see its keys. The edit therefore builds the ConfigDict from the class's non-dunder attributes, which keeps the keys unchanged as the finding requires. If ExampleConfigDefaults is itself a v1-style Config class whose attributes are not plain config keys, it should be checked, and it may need its own migration. The rest of the file (Field usage, LogLevel, handlers) has no v1 APIs that the findings flag, so it is left unchanged."}
